        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483322515",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": false,
        "description": "**About The Company**\n Software Technology, Inc. develops and delivers software solutions that help organizations address business needs through reliable, practical technology. Our work brings together engineering, product, and client\\-facing teams to build, improve, and support applications and digital services. We value thoughtful problem\\-solving, clear communication, dependable delivery, and a commitment to learning as technology and customer needs evolve. Team members have the opportunity to contribute ideas, collaborate across disciplines, and help shape solutions from initial discovery through ongoing improvement.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n Software Technology, Inc. is seeking a Software Engineer to design, develop, test, and maintain software applications. In this role, you will work with engineers, product stakeholders, and other colleagues to understand requirements and turn them into secure, maintainable, and usable solutions. You will contribute throughout the development lifecycle, from evaluating technical options and writing code to testing, deployment, and support. The ideal candidate is curious, accountable, and comfortable working through complex problems while keeping quality and user needs in view. This position requires sound technical judgment and the ability to explain decisions and progress to both technical and nontechnical partners.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n Candidates should have a bachelor’s degree in computer science, software engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience. Professional experience developing software in a collaborative environment is preferred. You should be familiar with at least one modern programming language and have a working understanding of software design principles, data structures, version control, and application testing. Experience with databases, APIs, cloud platforms, or automated build and deployment processes is beneficial. We also value familiarity with secure coding practices, accessibility considerations, and iterative development methods. Strong analytical skills, attention to detail, and a willingness to learn unfamiliar tools are important. You should be able to manage competing priorities, ask clear questions, receive feedback constructively, and work effectively both independently and as part of a team.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n Design, implement, review, and maintain software features based on business and user requirements. Collaborate with product and technical partners to clarify goals, assess feasibility, identify dependencies, and propose practical approaches. Write readable, reusable, and well\\-documented code in accordance with team standards. Develop and execute unit, integration, and other appropriate tests; investigate defects; and help resolve issues that affect reliability or performance. Participate in code reviews and share constructive feedback that supports quality and knowledge exchange. Contribute to technical documentation, estimates, design discussions, and planning activities. Follow established security, privacy, and data\\-handling practices, and raise potential risks promptly. Support releases and production systems by monitoring behavior, troubleshooting reported problems, and helping identify lasting improvements. Communicate progress, blockers, and technical considerations clearly, and stay current with relevant tools and practices.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Benefits**\n Software Technology, Inc. offers a collaborative environment where employees can contribute to meaningful software projects and continue developing their skills. Depending on eligibility and location, the overall rewards package may include competitive compensation, health and wellness coverage, paid time off, retirement savings options, and professional development support. Employees may also have access to opportunities for mentorship, cross\\-functional collaboration, and exposure to a range of technical challenges. Specific compensation, benefits, and work arrangements will be discussed during the hiring process and may vary based on role, location, and applicable employment terms.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Software Technology, Inc. is an equal opportunity employer. We make employment decisions without regard to legally protected characteristics and are committed to a respectful workplace where individuals are treated fairly. Applicants who need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process may contact the company to request support.",
